+## 14. Conversation list
+
+`list_conversations` is accepted independently of configuration and drops extra fields, including `userId`; optional `limit` is an integer from 1 through 200, and optional `before` is a composite cursor with a parseable date string `updatedAt` and string `sessionId`, with malformed fields refused by name ([validated by: validates history requests and composite cursors independently of configuration](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L97)).
+
+With history enabled, a request returns exactly one `conversation_list` with the authenticated connection user’s summaries in store order, only `sessionId`, ISO string `createdAt`, ISO string `updatedAt` and `entryCount`, forwarding `{limit, before}` to `listFor(ws.userId, options)` and emitting no `stream_end`; a listed id opens through the existing authenticated resume and replay path ([validated by: lists only the authenticated user metadata, forwards paging, and opens a listed conversation through resume](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L138)).
+
+History is opt-in through `transport.history.enabled`, independently of resume; absent or disabled history, a store without `listFor`, and a Mongo collection adapter without `find` all answer exactly one `UNSUPPORTED` error and no list ([validated by: refuses history with UNSUPPORTED when disabled or the store cannot list, without sending a list](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L178)).
+
+A failing list answers one sanitized `SERVER_ERROR`, keeps the socket usable, and logs the session id without store detail or user content ([validated by: returns a sanitized SERVER_ERROR and logs the session when a real store fails, keeping the socket usable](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L206)).
+
+A history request is answered outside the per-session turn lock, before a pending turn’s `stream_end`; lists are sent only on request, and include the current conversation ([validated by: answers a history request before stream_end while a turn holds the session lock and never pushes a list](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L219)).
+
+**GDPR.** The response exposes one authenticated user’s conversation metadata and no conversation content; the user id comes from the connection, never the frame. Enabling `transport.history` is the deployer’s decision to expose this personal data to a client; retention and erasure remain governed by the store and #41.
+
+| Request field | Type                                     | Required |
+| ------------- | ---------------------------------------- | -------- |
+| `type`        | `"list_conversations"`                   | Yes      |
+| `limit`       | integer 1–200                            | No       |
+| `before`      | `{updatedAt: string, sessionId: string}` | No       |
+
+| Response field  | Type                    | Description                                           |
+| --------------- | ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`          | `"conversation_list"`   | Requested history page                                |
+| `conversations` | `ConversationSummary[]` | Metadata rows, with both dates encoded as ISO strings |
